NPM is just package manager not "node package manager"
package.json is a configuration for npm, it takes care of all the packages/dependencies needed for the app
bundler will minify, clean, bundle, chunking etc basically make it production ready
DevDep: generally required in dev phase rather than being used for app running/functioning

^ => caret ~ => tild
^ will only upgrade to minor versions (thus usually safe to use this)
~ will upgrade to the major versions

package-lock will keep track of exact version installaed, package.json may contain approximate version with ~ or ^.

transitive dependencies: dependencies of dependencies needed for our app 

npx means executing any package using npm

